  {
   "commentType": "DISEASE",
   "note": {
    "texts": [
     {
      "value": "TBL2 is located in the Williams-Beuren syndrome (WBS) critical region. WBS results from a hemizygous deletion of several genes on chromosome 7q11.23, thought to arise as a consequence of unequal crossing over between highly homologous low-copy repeat sequences flanking the deleted region. Haploinsufficiency of TBL2 may be the cause of certain cardiovascular and musculo-skeletal abnormalities observed in the disease"
     }
    ]
   }
